# UI rules (V16–V20)

## V16 — Snapshot store, not log parsing

The dashboard reads from `internal/store` via REST/SSE.

Do not tail or parse `metrics-collector.log` for UI data.

## V17 — Non-blocking reads

API and SSE endpoints read from the store only. No collector or shell calls in HTTP handlers.

## V18 — Optional UI (headless mode)

- `METRICS_UI_ENABLED=false` must skip HTTP server and static SPA.
- Agent continues JSON log output and scheduling unchanged.

## V20 — i18n (no hardcoded UI strings)

- All user-visible text uses keys from `go/web/frontend/src/i18n/*.json`.
- Ship **en** and **tr**; add locales only with full key parity.
- Use `tool/check_i18n_coverage.sh` before merge when touching locale files.
- API field names (`cpuLoad`, …) stay English — translate labels only.

## Visual testing

- Layout, split-view, or scroll changes: run **ui-visual-review** skill (`make ui-visual-serve`, port **18081**).
- Container “agent dashboard” is tested via host `/container-metrics?id=…`, not container mapped port (Docker image may serve stale UI).
- CI: `make ui-e2e` — see `docs/VISUAL_TESTING.md`.

See `docs/UI_PLAN.md` for screen layout and API design.
